==Battleground==
*1 [[Gobble]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 16~20 seconds<sup>480f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Gobble]]s spawn, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**5 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 18.67~25.33 seconds<sup>560f~760f</sup>.
**3 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**2 [[Loris|Lorises]] spawn, delay 68~72 seconds<sup>2,040f~2,160f</sup>.

==Strategy==
In this stage, the only real pushers are the Brollows that spawn as Lowkey and Loris act more as chippers, and Gobble has a very long backswing, allowing your meatshields to just run back up the map. Because of this, you want to use units that one shot Brollow or at least deal a lot of damage at once. Units include [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] provides great defence against the Brollows and the Gobbles to some extent, while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is able to rush in and deal big damage to Gobble and potentially Lowkey.

Because Lowkey moves extremely slow, after killing the first Gobble and the first two Brollows, you can use Fishman to trigger the base and lure the first Loris to the base. Afterwards, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used to clear out the Brollows with his [[Explosion]] and rush down Loris. Be careful not to trigger Gobble's attack with any meatshields, as Bahamut might run in while Gobble is attacking and die before Loris does, which can prove annoying. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is as always a great bring to this stage, keeping the incredibly slow Gobble and Lowkey in place while chipping Loris and potentially syncing Brollows.

Research Combos also help a ton here when hitting Lowkey becomes impossible, especially in higher difficulties. Octopus Cat's [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immune]] Talent is perfect for said strategy.

===Recommended Ubers===

*[[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa, type Σ]]: A pretty solid pick here for an midranger. She has good bulk and a good slow up time, making the Brollows stay out of the battlefield. Furthermore, her [[Toxic Immunity]] and Curse basically makes Gobble a piece of cake and does quick work against Lowkey.

